      "issue": "The claim 'No line opening was authorized' is supported by text at 10:02 ('RHOB service issue under review. No line opening authorized'), but the node label implies a procedural condition that must be verified against an applicable requirement (e.g., LOTO or work-order rule) and evidence of what action occurred before its prerequisite. The current source only records the status 'No line opening authorized' without establishing whether this was due to pending authorization, lack of request, or explicit denial by authority.",
