      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim 'RHOB reported an air-low indication and requested Utilities attendance' is partially supported by the shift log entry at 10:00 ('Air-low indication. Local controls showing supply complaints. Requested Utilities attendance'). However, uncertainty remains about whether this refers strictly to alarm AL-44 trigger or just observed pressure trend (P-R). The point register shows P-R dropped below 5.8 bar and then further; the exact threshold for 'air-low' is not explicitly tied to a specific alarm state in the provided evidence.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record that defines what constitutes an 'air-low' indication: either a formal AL-44 trigger or operator observation of P-R below a defined limit. Evidence must clarify whether RHOB's report was based on alarm activation, visual inspection, or both.",
      "question": "Does the system define 'air-low' as triggered by AL-44 (below 5.0 bar) or does it rely on observed pressure trend? Was the 10:00 entry an automatic alarm acknowledgment or a manual observation?"
    },
    "node-2xniwn": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim 'Utilities acknowledged receipt of the issue at ~10:02 AM and paused work' is supported by shift log entries ('About 10:02 | Utilities | Work paused. RHOB service issue under review'). However, there is no explicit record confirming that Utilities formally acknowledged the origin or content of the notification; acknowledgment may be implicit in response sequence but not explicitly documented.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A communication log (radio transcript, digital message) showing an explicit acknowledgment from Utilities to RHOB at 10:02. Alternatively, a procedure defining whether 'Work paused' implicitly constitutes formal acknowledgment of the issue's origin and content.",
      "question": "Does the organization require written or verbal confirmation that Utilities acknowledged both receipt and understanding of the air-loss cause? Is there any record (radio log, digital ticket) showing such explicit acknowledgment at 10:02?"
    }
  },
